From 44614a68a082595497c7946ef0574f08e4160980 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:01:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add MRP and wholesale price levels

Variants get optional MRP and wholesale prices (0 = not set). Sales and POS
get a Retail/Wholesale level that seeds each line's price; items without a
wholesale price use retail, hand-edited line prices survive a level switch,
and the level resets to Retail after each confirmed sale. Posting RPCs are
untouched: they still take the price from the document line.

- migration 0037: two numeric columns; save_catalogue_variant regenerated
  from the 0033 body plus the two columns
- catalogue schema, edit-variant update, CSV export/import (MRP and
  Wholesale Price aliases) and the downloadable template
- products page: form fields, table columns, non-blocking price warnings
- supabase types updated by hand to match the migration
- tests: price-levels helper, CSV round trip; two exact-match expectations
  in inventory-schemas.test.ts now include the new fields

Not run: vitest and the CSV tests (vitest, papaparse and decimal.js are not
installable in this environment). Helper tests were run through a bun:test
shim; touched files were syntax-checked and the helper, schema and generated
types were type-checked under the repo's strict flags.

